pageType: twoColumn
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$paper"
notes: >-
  Alignment is cheap at the start and expensive later. Before the kickoff, two
  engineers and a designer can each believe the project is about something
  different. This kickoff forces one shared answer to three questions: what are
  we building, for whom, and what does done look like. Check: ask anyone in the
  room — they should answer those three questions in one breath. If they can't,
  the plan isn't aligned yet.
